        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'How it handles in the tree',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'The low-stretch build gives efficient ascents and a direct feel when you are moving laterally. Hitches set and release cleanly, and the smooth cover is easy on friction savers and cambium savers. The lighter weight is noticeable on long SRS lines and on big removals where you carry a lot of rope.',
            1 => 'Like any thinner, slicker line, it can run a little faster through some hitches than a thicker 16-strand. Test your hitch and adjust wraps or braids low in the tree before climbing high. Pair it with a <a href="/climbing/climbing-gear/ascent-and-descent/mechanical-friction-devices/devices-for-mrs/petzl-zigzag-mechanical-friction-device/">Petzl Zigzag</a> or similar only if the rope is within the device\'s listed range.',
            2 => 'On SRS the lighter weight is a real advantage. A long single line from a canopy anchor to the ground can be heavy to haul up for a basal tie or to drag around the tree. A thinner, lighter line makes those resets less tiring. On MRS, the smooth cover helps a micro pulley tend the hitch without hanging up.',
            3 => 'For a crew that standardizes on Poison Ivy, adding Poison Moon lets each climber have a distinct line while keeping hitch cords and devices the same across the crew.',
