          'h' => 'Inspection and retirement',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Check the full length before each climb for cover cuts, stiff or flattened sections, glazing from heat, and chemical contamination. Keep it in a bag and away from saw fuel, bar oil, and battery acid.',
            1 => 'Life-support gear must meet the applicable standard (ANSI Z133 and the manufacturer\'s instructions), be inspected before every climb, and be used only by trained climbers.',
            2 => 'If you work around sap-heavy species such as pine, clean sap off promptly; it stiffens the cover and changes how hitches grip. Store the rope loose in a bag rather than tightly coiled for long periods, and keep a record of when it went into service.',
