          1 => 'treeMOTION, treeMOTION Pro, treeMOTION evo',
        ),
      ),
      'body' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Why the treeMOTION Pro stands out',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'The treeMOTION family is one of the most popular saddle lines in tree care. The semi-rigid waist means the saddle does not fold or roll when you lean back, and the wide leg straps support you on long hangs. The Pro version adds refinements over the base model aimed at full-time climbers.',
            1 => 'The bridge setup is adjustable, and many parts are replaceable, which helps the saddle last through years of hard work.',
            2 => 'Climbers often mention how well the treeMOTION supports them during long hangs and removals. The semi-rigid waist spreads load, and the leg straps help keep pressure off the inside of the legs.',
            3 => 'Spend time adjusting the bridge and leg straps so the saddle sits right.',
          ),
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'h' => 'Fit and safety',
          'p' => 
          array (
            0 => 'Size carefully, adjust with your climbing clothes on, and hang test before you climb. Inspect the bridge, rings, buckles and webbing before each climb. Compare with the <a href="/climbing/saddles-and-harnesses/european-saddles/petzl-sequoia-climbing-harness/">Petzl Sequoia</a>.',
            1 => 'A saddle is life-support equipment: buy one that meets the applicable standard, follow the manufacturer\'s instructions and ANSI Z133, inspect it before every climb and retire it when wear reaches the maker\'s limits. Get trained before you climb on any new system.',
            2 => 'Accessories are a big part of the appeal. There are chest harness options, tool holders and replacement parts, so you can tune the saddle to your work as your climbing changes.',
          ),
        ),
      ),
      'faq' => 
      array (
        0 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'What is the difference between treeMOTION Pro and evo?',
          'a' => 'They are different generations and versions of the treeMOTION line with different features and parts. Check the specific model before ordering spares.',
        ),
        1 => 
        array (
          'q' => 'Is the treeMOTION harness good for SRS?',
          'a' => 'It works for SRS with the right setup and accessories, such as a chest harness. Follow Teufelberger\'s guidance.',
        ),
      ),
